{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SU2EmergenceRankForced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SU2EmergenceRankForced","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.su2_emergence_volume_determinant","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.no_three_dimensional_fundamental_in_one_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.no_three_dimensional_fundamental_in_one_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SU2EmergenceRankForced.lean#L125-L149","doc":"**A single fibre satisfying the volume constraint has no three-dimensional\nfundamental.**\n\nImmediate from `exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff`, and recorded separately because\nit is the form the flavour question needs: the eightfold-way sector requires a\nthree-dimensional `W`, and this says one fibre cannot supply it.\n\n**This is a SECOND route to a confinement the corpus already has, not a new\nresult.** `eightfold-open-problems` states — correctly — that *\"the search is\nconfined to the groupoid level is now a theorem, not an extrapolation\"*, on the\nstrength of the `Sym²` gate (`Sym2Gate.lean`, `Sym2GateParity.lean`): a\nthree-dimensional `W` must have `Sym²(W)` irreducible, and the gate decides\nthat for an irreducible summand.\n\nThe two arguments are independent. The `Sym²` route constrains `W` by the\nrepresentation theory of its symmetric square; this one constrains the *fibre*\nby the non-degeneracy of its volume form, and never mentions `W`'s symmetric\nsquare at all. Two independent derivations of the same negative is worth\nhaving; neither supplies the construction that is actually open, which is a\nthree-dimensional `W` in the **multi-fibre groupoid**. Nothing here bears on\nthat, and nothing here should be read as narrowing it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.volume_constraint_fails_of_not_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.volume_constraint_fails_of_not_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SU2EmergenceRankForced.lean#L117-L123","doc":"**Contrapositive form**: a fibre whose gauge group is not special unitary\nat rank 2 cannot satisfy the volume constraint. Recorded because this is the\ndirection a falsification would come from — exhibit a fibre automorphism\nviolating `det = 1` or `g·g† = 1`, and the volume form is what breaks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.su2_emergence_rank_hypothesis_is_load_bearing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.su2_emergence_rank_hypothesis_is_load_bearing","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SU2EmergenceRankForced.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**The rank conjunct is load-bearing, not decorative.**\n\nIf it followed from the unitarity half it would hold at every `N`. It does\nnot: at `N = 3` the volume hypothesis `exteriorSquareDim N = 1` is false\n(`dim Λ²V = 3`), so `su2_emergence_rank_forced` has no `N = 3` instance —\nwhile `mem_specialUnitary_of_unitary_of_det_one` applies at `N = 3` perfectly\nwell. That contrast is the anti-vacuity check: the two halves are independent,\nand only the volume constraint distinguishes rank 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.su2_emergence_rank_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.su2_emergence_rank_forced","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SU2EmergenceRankForced.lean#L84-L103","doc":"**`thm:su2-emergence` with the rank derived.**\n\nGiven the volume constraint in its strong form — `dim Λ²V = 1`, i.e.\n`Λ²V ≅ 𝟙` — and a set `G` of automorphisms of the fibre each preserving the\nvolume form (`det g = 1`) and the Frobenius dagger (`g · g† = 1`), BOTH\nconclusions follow:\n\n* `N = 2`, from the volume constraint alone; and\n* `G ⊆ SU(N)`, from the two constraints alone.\n\nThe conjunction is the statement `prf:su2-emergence` intended. Neither\nconjunct implies the other, which is why they are stated together. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:su2-emergence","label":"thm:su2-emergence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.mem_specialUnitary_of_unitary_of_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.mem_specialUnitary_of_unitary_of_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SU2EmergenceRankForced.lean#L73-L82","doc":"**The subgroup half is rank-free.** For any `n`, a unitary matrix of\ndeterminant one is special unitary. Stated at general `n` precisely to make\nvisible that this half carries no rank content — the `Fin 2` in\n`su2_emergence_combined` is an instance, not a consequence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}